nt planet  zdr and then launched a research unit  along with  seven emmy robots to apparently find and  extract the axe parasite  the research unit allegedly disappeared  once they arrived on the planet when  samus learned of all this  she said does the x truly still exist  and just what is happening on zdr  it's up to me the only one immune to the  x parasite  to go find out and then decided to fly  off to planet zdr and get involved with  all of this  of her own volition now it's possible  that the metroid devs are legitimately  just  adding in more x parasite on a new  unknown planet  kind of randomly but let's assume for  the time being that the chozo were  correct  when they researched and found that the  x parasite is only present on the planet  sr-388 and had not yet begun to  repopulate on other planets  after all that is the entire reasoning  behind their decision to contain the x  parasite to  its native planet and why they created  the metroids in the first place and  released them on said planet  if this is true then samus really did  rid the world of the x when she  destroyed the planet including everyone  and everything  on it and the biologic space station  which were the only two places in  existence that the x was present in  given that samus herself stated that the  federation would hold her accountable  for these actions and would not  understand her reasoning for destroying  the x and the federation's proven  history of secretive and even illegal  weapons projects  here's the big question that potentially  all of the events of metro dread are  centered around  what if the federation has lured samus  to this random remote planet of zdr  because she has the last remaining x  parasite within her own  dna and the emmy robots are supposed to  hunt  her what if metroid red is a trap for  the bounty hunter  think about it there are no living  galactic federation researchers or  scientists on the planet i'd imagine  just in case  samus blows it up again 